id: pm-q7qojt
title: "GH-793: remove or disambiguate list --all so filtered output cannot claim workspace completeness"
description: "The list --all alias controls pagination while the command defaults to open statuses, causing an intuitive all-workspace query to return only active rows and label the filtered result complete. Make scope and completeness explicit and token-safe."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-28T11:30:12.179Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T15:58:52.279Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T16:27:55.507Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Bare --all cannot silently mean only no-truncate; callers receive either a clear error suggesting --status all or an unambiguous replacement; completeness distinguishes full workspace scope from post-filter pagination; total semantics are documented and tested across JSON and TOON; aliases and runtime contracts remain aligned
goal: project management = context management
objective: Prevent agents from confidently treating a filtered list as the complete project timeline
value: All-status project context becomes explicit and trustworthy
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: All-status scope and pagination completeness are explicit and unambiguous.
actual_result: Deprecated --all now errors with exact --status all and --no-truncate migration commands.
